    431  f259							; Op 4 TITLE (every title frame, no I2C): the HUD score window shows the 1-based
    432  f259							; stage number (packed BCD, 000001 = stage 1) and, for 64 of every 256 frames
    433  f259							; (EnemyRamP $80-$BF; it restarts at $F0 on every LoadLevel, so SELECT always
    434  f259							; shows the stage first), the HIGH SCORE BOOT left in SkHi. No high score (no key,
    435  f259							; blank chip) = the stage number only. DropArm's title path writes the same stage
    436  f259							; number once per LoadLevel (SELECT); this keeps it right in between.
    437  f259				   SkTitle
    438  f259		       a5 a3		      lda	Level
    439  f25b		       18		      clc
    440  f25c		       69 01		      adc	#1
    441  f25e		       a2 00		      ldx	#0
    442  f260				   .SkTen
    443  f260		       c9 0a		      cmp	#10
    444  f262		       90 05		      bcc	.SkOnes
    445  f264		       e9 0a		      sbc	#10
    446  f266		       e8		      inx
    447  f267		       d0 f7		      bne	.SkTen	; (X <= 2: always taken)
    448  f269				   .SkOnes
